terraform workspace new dev    - dev workspace created
terraform workspace list
terraform workspace select dev
git checkout -b dev
git status
git init
git add .
git commit -m "added terraform"     #terraform and git git both are on dev branch


now we can filter in aws console -  instances> Environment=dev     - dev branch/workspace instances showing 
    and in ec2.tf also give tag like 
tags = {
  Name        = each.key
  Environment = var.env                 - #env will pick from var.tf
}

same we can create for prod also and update in variable.tf also 

variable.tf .......................
variable "env" {
  default = "dev"
  type = string
}


scenario 2 for prod--------------------------------------------->>
terraform workspace new prod  
terraform workspace select prod
terraform workspace show
git checkout -b prod
var.tf - give prod  
do whatever changes you want change any instance type or something else
git add .
git commit
teraform validate
terraform apply 
terraform state list -   fr diff-diff as per env
go to aws instances > search Environment = prod   - only prod instance will be showing

**** by this we can separately manage our multi environment using same code using git and terraform workspace. diff diff state file is maintaning in diff diff env.
